    "wholeText": "# Printable text model cards / Druckbare Text-Modellkarten\n\nSkillPilot authored candidate, CC-BY-4.0. This is a text working kit, not a new\nlearning-goal image or a programme-generated SVG. Printing/learner use has not\nbeen performed or accepted.\n\n## Lower material/reaction kit / Unteres Materie-/Reaktionsset\n\nPrepare labelled paper tokens / beschriftete Papierkarten bereitstellen:\n4 × H, 2 × O; 6 × Na⁺, 6 × Cl⁻; 8 × H–O–H cards, with O end negative and H\nends positive. Keep particle species/charge visible. A solid/lattice region,\nsolution region and reaction-arrangement region are labelled on blank paper.\nDo not present tokens as physical atom photographs.\n\n## Upper organic kit / Oberes organisches Set\n\nProvide paper/physical molecular segments for the hypothetical scaffold\n⁺H3N–CH2–CH2–C(=O)–NH–CH2–C6H5. Labels identify ammonium, carbonyl oxygen,\namide plane and phenyl plane. A teacher-supplied spatial kit/cards must expose\ntetrahedral versus planar regions; a flat text chain alone is not the spatial\nperformance. Provide receptor contact labels: negative / negativ,\nhydrogen-bond donor / H-Brücken-Donor, hydrophobic / hydrophob.\nTwo posed versions L and L2 can be physically arranged; L2 is deliberately\nmisaligned. Learner arrangement is retained as own work, not prefilled here.\n\n## Substrate/enzyme kit / Substrat-/Enzymset\n\nS: R–C(=O)–O–R′ ; H2O; E contact model able to adjust; ES combined state;\nP1: R–C(=O)–OH ; P2: R′–OH; inhibitor I binds without conversion.\nUse reversible binding and a separate conversion arrow; release E after\nconversion. This is a simplified model, not real protein or clinical proof.\n",
    "boundary": "Only lower matter/reaction cards relevant; original whole kit retained as history; no completed learner model product."
  },
